      "writtenOn": "2022-06-08T22:19:31Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Why are we using the `location` qualifier here for an array but the `binding` qualifier for textures2D (e.g. in Desaturate.compute)?\n\nThese unsized buffers and textures are both global shader resources and `binding` would make sense in both situations. Granted, the way GLSL uses `location` to mean different things across varyings and global uniforms is already inconsistent but I would prefer if we were consistent in how we declare global resources.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 1,
        "startChar": 7,
        "endLine": 1,
        "endChar": 15
      },
      "revId": "39434936f3ef13ec8665cb3eecee754710b70420",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "6a5277e8_e18317f3",
        "filename": "resources/sksl/compute/ArrayAdd.compute",
        "patchSetId": 16
      },
      "lineNbr": 1,
      "author": {
        "id": 5640
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-06-09T15:02:26Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "The location in this case purely specifies the order in which the parameters appear in the compute shader\u0027s parameters. Textures are a different beast.",
      "parentUuid": "4fcb37c6_4c9fa777",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 1,
        "startChar": 7,
        "endLine": 1,
        "endChar": 15
      },
      "revId": "39434936f3ef13ec8665cb3eecee754710b70420",
